From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 08:14:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] clk: samsung: exynos9820: Add the CMU_DPU and CMU_CMGP blocks

CMU_DPU gates the DECON, the DMA of the DPP channels, the APB bus of
DSIM0 and the three display System MMUs. CMU_CMGP gates the I2C
controller the display PMIC hangs off. Neither block exists in the port
tree the driver came from, so without them the whole display path has no
clock provider: decon0, dsim0, the three sysmmu nodes and i2c@15d50000
would never probe.

Base addresses, mux and divider layout, gate offsets, field widths and
the parent of every gate are transcribed from the vendor clock
abstraction layer tables
(drivers/soc/samsung/cal-if/exynos9820/cmucal-sfr.c and cmucal-node.c of
LineageOS/android_kernel_samsung_exynos9820 at 7d08ec364a06).

Every offset, every gate bit and every mux and divider field above was
checked against those tables, field by field, before it was written here.

CMU_CMGP holds its own APB clock on with CLK_IS_CRITICAL, the way every
other always on block in this driver does. CMU_DPU does not, and that
asymmetry is deliberate: it sits in a power domain that is switched off
whenever the display is idle, and a critical clock would keep the domain
from ever going down.

UNVERIFIED: which gates are held on and which may be gated is a decision
taken here rather than a vendor statement, and it has not been checked
on hardware. It is listed as an open question in the porting notes.

Signed-off-by: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/clk/samsung/clk-exynos9820.c | 752 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 752 insertions(+)

